---
// The site's privacy policy. Every statement here is a fact about the site's own code
// (src/scripts/theme.ts for the stored settings, Pagefind for search, no third-party requests);
// change this page in the same PR as any change that makes one of them untrue.
import Site from '../../layouts/Site.astro';
import {
  CONTACT_EMAIL,
  ORG_NAME,
  ORG_URL,
  REPO_URL,
  SITE_NAME,
  SITE_URL,
} from '../../data/site';

const UPDATED = '2026-10-21';
const updatedText = new Date(`${UPDATED}T00:00:00Z`).toLocaleDateString('en', {
  day: 'numeric',
  month: 'long',
  year: 'numeric',
  timeZone: 'UTC',
});
const host = new URL(SITE_URL).host;
---

<Site
  title="Privacy policy"
  description={`How ${SITE_NAME} handles your data: no cookies, analytics or ads, theme settings kept in your browser, search that runs on your device.`}
>
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p class="site-lead">
    This site doesn't use cookies, analytics or advertising, and it never asks for personal
    information. Your theme settings stay in your browser.
  </p>
  <p>Last updated <time datetime={UPDATED}>{updatedText}</time>.</p>

  <h2 id="who">Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE_NAME} ({host}) is the documentation site of the open-source <code>@kyralabs</code> packages,
    run by <a href={ORG_URL}>{ORG_NAME}</a>. This policy covers this site only.
  </p>

  <h2 id="hosting">When you visit</h2>
  <p>
    The site is a set of static pages hosted on <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/">Cloudflare</a>
    Pages. To deliver the pages and protect them against abuse, Cloudflare processes the technical
    data your browser sends with every request: your IP address, the page you asked for, your
    browser's user agent and the time. Cloudflare handles this data under the
    <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare privacy policy</a>. {ORG_NAME} adds
    no analytics, tracking or logging of its own, and doesn't use this data to identify visitors.
    Cloudflare may show us aggregate figures, such as the number of requests.
  </p>
  <p>
    Fonts, icons, scripts, images and the search index all come from this site. Pages make no
    requests to other services: no web fonts from Google, no CDNs, no embeds.
  </p>

  <h2 id="cookies">Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    The site sets no cookies. Cloudflare may set a strictly necessary security cookie when it needs
    to check that a request comes from a person rather than a bot.
  </p>

  <h2 id="storage">What's stored in your browser</h2>
  <p>
    When you change the color theme, the site remembers your choice in your browser's local storage
    so that every page uses it. Nothing in local storage is sent to us or to anyone else.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <code>m3e-site:mode</code>: light or dark, if you picked one in the theme menu. Choosing System
      removes it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>m3e-site:theme-seed</code> and <code>m3e-site:theme-css</code>: the seed color and the
      generated theme, if you applied one from the home page or the color theme builder. Resetting
      the theme on the home page removes them.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>You can also delete them at any time by clearing this site's data in your browser settings.</p>

  <h2 id="search">Search</h2>
  <p>
    Search runs on your device. The search box downloads the site's index from this site and looks
    up your words in your browser; what you type is never sent anywhere.
  </p>

  <h2 id="packages">The packages themselves</h2>
  <p>
    The <code>@kyralabs</code> packages you install from npm contain no telemetry and make no network
    requests. Fonts and icons are files you serve from your own site.
  </p>

  <h2 id="links">Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    Pages link to other sites, such as GitHub, npm, the playground and material.io. Their own privacy
    policies apply once you follow a link.
  </p>

  <h2 id="rights">Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Because {ORG_NAME} doesn't collect or store personal data about visitors, there is normally
    nothing for us to give you a copy of, correct or delete. For data Cloudflare processes, you can
    use the rights described in Cloudflare's policy. If you have a question or a request, contact us
    as below.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If the site changes how it handles data, this page changes with it and the date above is
    updated. Every earlier version is in the <a href={`${REPO_URL}/commits/main/apps/site/src/pages/privacy/index.astro`}
      >history of this page</a
    > on GitHub.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>
    For questions about this policy or a privacy request, email {ORG_NAME} at
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. Please don't put personal details in a
    public <a href={`${REPO_URL}/issues`}>GitHub issue</a>; issues are for questions about the
    library itself.
  </p>
</Site>
